;; repr/ocaml's print level's divergences (bin/reap's OCaml print cell; doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, "As built: O8 (write-ahead)"):
;; the classes every file of test/ocaml/print-results.edn that does not pass falls into, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format,
;; matched against "RESULT REASON" as the record writes them. A printer's failure (fail: not printed, printed text the oracle
;; rejects, a print not stable) is never recorded and the cell refuses it whatever its class. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :string-bytes
  :title "string literals whose bytes the :lines printer did not keep: a CR LF in a quoted string, a byte that is not UTF-8"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "testsuite/tests/lexing/newlines.ml holds a quoted string whose value is CR LF, which the :lines print wrote as it is (the reprint's lexer reads \"\\n\": lexer.mll's store_normalized_newline removes one CR); re's lib_test/expect/test_pcre.ml a quoted string with the byte 255, which the forms carry as a byte vector the printer wrote as its text. Fixed by OC214 (a) (the user, 2026-11-10: the quoted string's CR LF written CR CR LF, its bytes written as they are; the round trip's trees equal for both, bin/repr-ocaml roundtrip --text --only-list): the rows keep this class until the next --record-results of the testsuite and opam-re corpora, which records newlines.ml a pass and test_pcre.ml mode :full's rejection (:full-not-utf8)"
  :decided "O2, O7 (\"As built\": recorded in test/ocaml/roundtrip-known.edn as :diff); O8; OC214 (a), 2026-11-10"
  :tests ["testsuite/testsuite/tests/lexing/newlines.ml" "opam-re/re/lib_test/expect/test_pcre.ml"]
  :match []}
 {:id :full-not-utf8
  :title "files that are not UTF-8: mode :full's layout, whose text is the tokens' strings, refuses them"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "mode :full keeps the file's text as the layout's strings (ocdump's tokens_form and the native layout alike refuse a file that is not valid UTF-8: test/ocaml/full-known.edn's :not-utf8); re's lib_test/expect/test_pcre.ml (the byte 255 in an [%expect] string) passes the :lines level since OC214 (a) but not the byte-for-byte text level. A layout of bytes (the printer's byte marks, OC214's text-bytes) would carry it: not done"
  :decided "OC214 (a), 2026-11-10 (its residue)"
  :match [#"^reject not-utf8 encoding: "]}]
